#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179521 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179666 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition Using a Difference of Squares"}] :question/id #uuid "500e1ff1-1a58-57f5-8d85-32ff78dafb35" :question/math-academy-id "e-6117" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[4, 6]$\n\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 6]$\n\nCalculate  $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j,$ where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[2, 6].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=6-2=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we can evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})+({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at \n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j = 20\\cdot 4 = 80.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179584 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/id #uuid "e2f01953-2fb1-5ddb-83ae-5d8a73e7f7ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-9482" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1, 2]$\n\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 3]$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n {3} \\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j,$ where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\Delta x_i$ and $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[-1, 2]$ and $[2,3]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =2-(-1)=3, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =3-2=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n3 \\sum_{i=1}^m \\Delta x_i \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = 9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526042 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "294c3cc6-d662-53c9-b36e-6a5692b9f4aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525306} {:answer/id #uuid "2fb1fc71-c6c9-501e-95e7-d1d36b4e13d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525319} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb97fb7-9081-5e35-a39a-0d9ff39f247c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525602} {:answer/id #uuid "afe570cc-99d0-5bbc-a39e-c80b3ab0abf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525650} {:answer/id #uuid "b26a0da6-fba9-5626-a287-a7c4aa41e02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "294c3cc6-d662-53c9-b36e-6a5692b9f4aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525306} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb3c82ed-1671-54bd-8e2d-7967feacedd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "77ce5f28-3326-5c6e-a417-40662b67aeff" :question/math-academy-id "q-123067" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,3]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,6]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[1,3]$ and $[3,6]$ respectively. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =3-1=2, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =6-3=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567057 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28ea07d6-a74d-513b-9ab7-f39585563779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566451} {:answer/id #uuid "4a9f8fc9-2e7e-5bcb-a049-e5cbe9e4b982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566507} {:answer/id #uuid "6a1579ff-aa71-5707-a7fe-fdcda8428378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566563} {:answer/id #uuid "d033888f-ccd5-545f-a93a-ac765f8a371c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566775} {:answer/id #uuid "d3ff4064-4f5c-588c-8bee-0c5e70b99376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a9f8fc9-2e7e-5bcb-a049-e5cbe9e4b982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566507} :answer-field/id #uuid "15497909-bf1d-5d2c-b840-2895c68c1424" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8220dea1-824f-5378-8691-0472e03156fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-123068" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[0,4]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,8]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[0,4]$ and $[2,8]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =4-0=4, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =8-2=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=4\\cdot 6=24.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "265ebb5d-6013-56b6-a1e4-0de08d94c7d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525297} {:answer/id #uuid "84f8b00f-5a24-5b47-a712-2790b187c427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525540} {:answer/id #uuid "912a022d-f6b3-50b7-a153-046e3669ebda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525573} {:answer/id #uuid "92d533f1-23d6-567a-9a29-1fd69535565d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #ed